            <ArticleTitle>Prostaglandin levels in endometrial jet wash specimens in patients with dysmenorrhea before and after indomethacin therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1047-56</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with functional primary dysmenorrhea of over two years duration was subjected to the endometrial jet wash technique during the period of active menstrual flow. Prostaglandin F analysis of the jet washings revealed significantly elevated levels during menstruation over normal control levels. Following indomethacin therapy, jet wash prostaglandin F levels were dramatically reduced and the patient became asymptomatic. A cause and effect relationsship between prostaglandin F and dysmenorrhea is suggested by these studied.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
